1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
LabWeaver connects a Container C/C++ lab and a KubeVirt Linux systems lab in one course journey.

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:19,500
The film stays inside the product; build identity and engineering evidence live in the manifest and final report.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The teacher uploads public-safe material and reviews the LLM egress and protected-content policy first.

4
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Two AgentRuns independently produce Environment and Evaluation candidates; waiting is compressed at observable succeeded states.

5
00:01:31,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The teacher reviews, explains, and approves each candidate; LLM advice cannot alter deterministic scores or bypass approval.

6
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Publishing creates immutable releases with controlled Runtime identity and deterministic validation results.

7
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:20,000
The platform administrator handles a resource request pre-created through the formal Work/Agent flow.

8
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:59,000
After approval, ResourceQuota and Lease terminal state are read back; no missing research-request UI is fabricated.

9
00:04:00,000 --> 00:05:10,000
The student creates a Container environment from a published template and receives a time-bounded AccessGrant after ready.

10
00:05:11,000 --> 00:06:59,000
The terminal sequence covers editing, compiling, and running the public sample, plus resize, reconnect, and lifecycle state.

11
00:07:00,000 --> 00:08:20,000
The student launches a real KubeVirt VM in the same course and enters Linux through the controlled noVNC endpoint.

12
00:08:21,000 --> 00:10:29,000
After the operation, stop/start or recovery is performed and the environment identity is checked across recovery.

13
00:10:30,000 --> 00:11:44,000
The workspace is frozen and its Object Version and SHA-256 are read back; only implemented terminal projections are shown.

14
00:11:45,000 --> 00:12:35,000
The teacher revokes the AccessGrant; the existing session must close and capability expires with the revision.

15
00:12:36,000 --> 00:13:14,000
A reconnect is explicitly refused with a stable diagnostic; network reachability never replaces authorization.

16
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:59,500
The student deletes the environment and verifies residue-free cleanup, completing the journey from authoring to safe reclamation.
